---
// PlatformBuilder.astro — "Primitive, not platform" four-layer stack
---

<section id="platform-builder" class="pb-section section-pad">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="pb-header" data-reveal>
      <span class="section-eyebrow">THE MISSING LAYER</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">
        The inner harness is getting absorbed. The outer runtime is still missing.
      </h2>
      <p class="pb-desc">
        Models and SDKs increasingly own the inner loop &mdash; call, tool, observe, repeat. The layer around it stays unsolved: recovery, sandboxes, approvals, replay, cheap waiting. Keep your SSO, RBAC, cloud accounts, and agent SDKs. Kitaru fills the gap.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pb-stack">

      <div class="pb-layer pb-layer-model" data-reveal="fade-up" data-reveal-delay="1">
        <div class="pb-layer-head">
          <span class="pb-layer-label">Model layer</span>
          <span class="pb-layer-role">reasoning and native tool-use behavior</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pb-layer-tags">
          <span class="pb-tag">OpenAI</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">Anthropic</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">Google</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">Open-weights</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">Fine-tuned in-house</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-ghost">your pick</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="pb-layer pb-layer-harness" data-reveal="fade-up" data-reveal-delay="2">
        <div class="pb-layer-head">
          <span class="pb-layer-label">Harness layer</span>
          <span class="pb-layer-role">the inner loop around the model</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pb-layer-tags">
          <span class="pb-tag">Pydantic AI / Harness</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">LangGraph</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">Claude Agent SDK</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">OpenAI Agents SDK</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">Raw Python</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-ghost">your pick</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="pb-layer pb-layer-kitaru" data-reveal="fade-up" data-reveal-delay="3">
        <div class="pb-layer-head">
          <span class="pb-layer-label">Runtime layer</span>
          <span class="pb-layer-role"><strong>Kitaru</strong> &mdash; the outer runtime</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pb-layer-tags">
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-accent">checkpoints</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-accent">replay</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-accent">resume</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-accent">wait()</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-accent">isolated execution</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-accent">versions + tag routing</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-accent">invocation</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-accent">artifacts + state</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pb-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="pb-layer pb-layer-platform" data-reveal="fade-up" data-reveal-delay="4">
        <div class="pb-layer-head">
          <span class="pb-layer-label">Platform layer</span>
          <span class="pb-layer-role">how the org governs and exposes agents</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pb-layer-tags">
          <span class="pb-tag">auth</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">entitlements</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">interceptors</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">guardrails</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">observability</span>
          <span class="pb-tag">product UI</span>
          <span class="pb-tag pb-tag-ghost">yours, unchanged</span>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="pb-why-grid">
      <div class="why-card" data-reveal="scale-up" data-reveal-delay="3">
        <div class="card-glow"></div>
        <div class="why-card-image">
          <img src="https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/34447ad2/k-prob-1-800.avif" srcset="https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/2cc2883d/k-prob-1-sm.avif 664w, https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/34447ad2/k-prob-1-800.avif 800w" alt="Durable agent state" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="400" height="225" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
        </div>
        <div class="why-card-content">
          <span class="why-card-tag">Recovery</span>
          <h3>Agent died at hour 11? Resume from hour 10.</h3>
          <p>Every durable checkpoint persists its inputs and outputs. Fix the failure and replay from the boundary that broke instead of re-running every model call and tool call upstream.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="why-card" data-reveal="scale-up" data-reveal-delay="4">
        <div class="card-glow"></div>
        <div class="why-card-image">
          <img src="https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/80283a6e/k-prob-2-800.avif" srcset="https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/bfd1b9bd/k-prob-2-sm.avif 664w, https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/80283a6e/k-prob-2-800.avif 800w" alt="One agent, three runtimes" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="400" height="225" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
        </div>
        <div class="why-card-content">
          <span class="why-card-tag">Trust boundaries</span>
          <h3>The brain and the hand should not share a process.</h3>
          <p>Run risky tools in controlled execution targets while the durable runner owns state, replay, and policy hooks. A sandbox failure becomes one failed checkpoint, not a lost agent.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="why-card" data-reveal="scale-up" data-reveal-delay="5">
        <div class="card-glow"></div>
        <div class="why-card-image">
          <img src="https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/79a5c5af/k-prob-3-800.avif" srcset="https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/71979af8/k-prob-3-sm.avif 664w, https://assets.kitaru.ai/content/site/79a5c5af/k-prob-3-800.avif 800w" alt="Runs you can actually compare" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="400" height="225" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 33vw" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
        </div>
        <div class="why-card-content">
          <span class="why-card-tag">Cheap waiting</span>
          <h3>Wait on humans, webhooks, or agents without burning compute.</h3>
          <p><code>wait()</code> suspends the run and releases the worker. When the input arrives minutes, hours, or days later, Kitaru rehydrates the execution and continues.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pb-callout" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="4">
      <p class="pb-callout-line">
        Kitaru isn&rsquo;t an agent platform. It&rsquo;s the runtime layer your platform runs agents on.
      </p>
      <p class="pb-callout-sub">
        Kubernetes can restart a pod. It cannot replay an agent from checkpoint 10 or wait three days for a human approval without burning compute.
      </p>
      <p class="pb-callout-sub">
        Bundled agent platforms ship one model, one harness, one cloud. Kitaru is the open assembled stack &mdash; same primitives, your stack.
      </p>
      <p class="pb-callout-sub">
        Open source. Self-hosted. No lock-in to a model, harness, or platform.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .pb-section {
    background: var(--color-accent-light);
  }

  .pb-header {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .pb-desc {
    margin-top: 16px;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  /* ─── Three-layer stack ─── */

  .pb-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  .pb-layer {
    position: relative;
    padding: 22px 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    transition: border-color 0.25s, transform 0.25s;
  }

  .pb-layer-model,
  .pb-layer-harness,
  .pb-layer-platform {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    opacity: 0.92;
  }

  .pb-layer-kitaru {
    border-color: oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.45);
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.08) 0%,
      oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.04) 100%
    );
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.15),
      0 12px 28px -18px oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.35);
    padding: 30px 32px;
  }

  .pb-layer-kitaru::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -1px;
    top: -1px;
    bottom: -1px;
    width: 4px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 14px 0 0 14px;
  }

  .pb-layer-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .pb-layer-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .pb-layer-kitaru .pb-layer-label {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .pb-layer-role {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .pb-layer-role strong {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-right: 4px;
  }

  .pb-layer-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .pb-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--color-surface-warm);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .pb-tag-accent {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    background: oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.1);
    border-color: oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.3);
  }

  .pb-tag-ghost {
    background: transparent;
    border-style: dashed;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Connector dots between layers */
  .pb-connector {
    align-self: center;
    width: 2px;
    height: 18px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      transparent 0%,
      var(--color-border) 40%,
      var(--color-border) 60%,
      transparent 100%
    );
  }

  /* ─── Callout ─── */

  .pb-callout {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding: 32px 36px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.04);
    border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
  }

  .pb-callout-line {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .pb-callout-line em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  .pb-callout-line strong {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .pb-callout-sub {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* ─── Why-cards grid (folded in from former ProblemStatement) ─── */
  .pb-why-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }

  .why-card-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    padding: 3px 9px;
    background: oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.08);
    border: 1px solid oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.2);
    border-radius: 100px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .pb-why-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .pb-layer {
      padding: 18px 20px;
    }
    .pb-layer-kitaru {
      padding: 22px 22px;
    }
    .pb-callout {
      padding: 24px 22px;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { setupCardGlow } from '../scripts/card-glow';
  setupCardGlow('.pb-section .why-card');
</script>
